@prefix : <https://w3id.org/ci#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix xml: <http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@base <https://w3id.org/ci#> .

<https://w3id.org/ci> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                      owl:imports <https://w3id.org/cterm> ;
                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> "Cassandro, J., Hagedorn, P., Sigalov, K., Gatto, C., Mirarchi, C., Pavan, A., & König, M. (2025). Semantic Integration of Cost, Time and Geometry for a Resource-centred Perspective of Managing Construction Projects: . Proceedings of the 2025 European Conference on Computing in Construction. Publiziert. European Conference on Computing in Construction, Porto. https://doi.org/10.35490/ec3.2025.263" ;
                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/contributor> _:genid1 ,
                                                             _:genid3 ;
                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-10-12"^^xsd:date ;
                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> _:genid5 ,
                                                         _:genid7 ;
                                                         
                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract> "The Cost Item (CI) Ontology provides a semantic model for representing and structuring construction cost items and their constituent components. It separates physical works from construction activities and supports the description of cost information through standardized terminology, quantitative attributes, units, and economic information. CI is designed to interoperate with the Construction Resources (CR) and Construction Terminology (CTERM) ontologies."@en ;                                                        
                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/abstract> "L'ontologia Cost Item (CI) fornisce un modello semantico per rappresentare e strutturare le voci di costo delle costruzioni e le relative componenti. Distingue le opere fisiche dalle attività di costruzione e supporta la descrizione delle informazioni di costo mediante terminologia standardizzata, attributi quantitativi, unità di misura e informazioni economiche. CI è progettata per interoperare con le ontologie Construction Resources (CR) e Construction Terminology (CTERM)."@it ;

                      <https://w3id.org/widoco/vocab> "Construction cost information is commonly represented through natural-language descriptions and catalogue-specific coding systems, which limits interoperability, automated querying, and reuse across digital construction workflows. The Cost Item (CI) Ontology addresses this issue by providing a structured semantic representation of construction cost items and their constituent components. The model distinguishes the physical entity involved in a construction result from the activity performed and represents each cost item through structured CostComponents. CI uses controlled terminology provided by the Construction Terminology (CTERM) Ontology and can be integrated with the Construction Resources (CR) Ontology to describe the elementary resources involved in construction production processes."@en ;
                      <https://w3id.org/widoco/vocab> "Le informazioni relative ai costi delle costruzioni sono comunemente rappresentate mediante descrizioni in linguaggio naturale e sistemi di codifica specifici dei singoli prezzari, limitando l'interoperabilità, l'interrogazione automatica e il riutilizzo dei dati nei processi digitali delle costruzioni. L'ontologia Cost Item (CI) affronta questo problema fornendo una rappresentazione semantica strutturata delle voci di costo e delle relative componenti. Il modello distingue l'entità fisica coinvolta nel risultato della costruzione dall'attività eseguita e rappresenta ciascuna voce attraverso CostComponent strutturati. CI utilizza la terminologia controllata fornita dall'ontologia Construction Terminology (CTERM) e può essere integrata con l'ontologia Construction Resources (CR) per descrivere le risorse elementari coinvolte nei processi produttivi delle costruzioni."@it ;

                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "The Cost Item (CI) Ontology is based on concepts and principles of construction project cost estimation and can be used together with the Construction Resources (CR) ontology and can use terminology from the Construction Terminology (CTERM)."@en ;
                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "L'ontologia Cost Item (CI) si basa su concetti e principi della stima dei costi dei progetti di costruzione e può essere utilizzata insieme all'ontologia Construction Resources (CR), utilizzando la terminologia della Construction Terminology (CTERM)."@it ;
                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-10-12"^^xsd:date ;
                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/rights> "Copyright 2025 by DABC, PoliMi" ;
                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "The Cost Item (CI) Ontology"@en ;
                      <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> "ci" ;
                      <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceUri> : ;
                      owl:versionInfo "0.3" ;
                      <https://schema.org/codeRepository> <https://github.com/cpm-ont-network/cost> .

